          "parts": [
            "We are given the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + A = \\frac{B}{C}\n\\]\n\nand the values:\n\n- \\( B = 5.65 \\)\n- \\( C = 0.510998950 \\)\n\n### Step 1: Solve for \\( A \\)\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{B}{C} - 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Plug in the values\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{5.65}{0.510998950} - 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nA \\approx 11.05836756 - 1 = 10.05836756\n\\]\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n\\[\nA \\approx \\boxed{10.0584}\n\\]\n\nWould you like this rounded to a specific number of decimal places?"
          ]
